{"id":"B2-L116","title":"Modal Perfect — possibility — production and review","cefr":"B2","level":"B2","unit":"B2-U07","focus":"Modal Perfect — possibilidade — produção e revisão","targets":{"grammar":"Modal Perfect — possibilidade — produção e revisão","pron":"Flap T americano","verbs":[],"pv":[],"expr":[],"words":["misplaced speech","coat pocket","mayor’s aide","office search","speech draft","podium note","campaign car","panic moment","lost document","secretary’s desk","tidy shelf","hallway whisper","city hall corridor","ceremony delay","mistaken guess","funny ending","story clue","plot suspense","short fiction","opening line"],"field":"Política como tema de discussão","genre":"Conto e trecho de peça","skill":"Escrita","words_min":20},"frames":[{"tag":"Abertura","title":"Lesson 116 · Modal Perfect — possibility — production and review","blocks":[{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Nesta aula","body":["**Foco:** Modal Perfect — possibilidade — produção e revisão.","**Pronúncia:** Flap T americano.","**20 palavras novas** (política como tema de discussão).","**Texto do dia:** conto e trecho de peça."]},{"type":"p","t":"**Objetivo de comunicação (B2):** eu consigo produzir um conto curto com modal perfect (might have, could have) para especular sobre o que aconteceu."},{"type":"box","kind":"exam","t":"Ponte para as provas","body":["","Esta aula treina **escrever frases claras e corretas (IELTS Writing, TOEFL Writing)**."]}]},{"tag":"Aquecimento","title":"Warm-up · Say the words","blocks":[{"type":"p","t":"Toque em 🔊, ouça e repita cada palavra. Depois tente adivinhar o sentido."},{"type":"words","items":[["misplaced speech","discurso extraviado"],["coat pocket","bolso do casaco"],["mayor’s aide","assessora do prefeito"],["office search","busca no escritório"],["speech draft","rascunho do discurso"],["podium note","nota de pódio"],["campaign car","carro de campanha"],["panic moment","momento de pânico"],["lost document","documento perdido"],["secretary’s desk","mesa da secretária"],["tidy shelf","prateleira arrumada"],["hallway whisper","sussurro no corredor"],["city hall corridor","corredor da prefeitura"],["ceremony delay","atraso da cerimônia"],["mistaken guess","palpite errado"],["funny ending","final engraçado"],["story clue","pista da história"],["plot suspense","suspense do enredo"],["short fiction","ficção curta"],["opening line","primeira frase"]]}]},{"tag":"Leitura","title":"Reading · A short story","blocks":[{"type":"text","title":"Short Story: The Missing Speech","paras":["The mayor’s speech was gone. Someone **might have taken** it, or she **could have left** it in the car. “It **may have fallen** behind the desk,” said her aide. “It **can’t have vanished**.”","They found it in the mayor’s coat pocket. “I **must have put** it there,” she laughed. “We **could have saved** an hour!”"],"kicker":"STORY","by":"Short Fiction Club","gloss":[["aide","assessor"],["vanish","desaparecer"],["pocket","bolso"],["speech","discurso"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"The speech was found in the mayor’s coat pocket.","ans":"T","why":"coat pocket."},{"q":"The aide thought someone had definitely stolen it.","ans":"F","why":"might have taken."},{"q":"The mayor laughed about it.","ans":"T","why":"laughed."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“aide” = ?","opts":["assessor","ajuda","ar"],"ans":0,"why":"aide."},{"q":"“vanish” = ?","opts":["desaparecer","vender","vazar"],"ans":0,"why":"vanish."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Modal Perfect — revisão","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Forma","Exemplo"],"rows":[["might / may have","Someone **might have taken** it."],["could have","She **could have left** it in the car."],["can’t have","It **can’t have vanished**."],["must have","I **must have put** it there."]],"cap":"Modal Perfect — revisão"},{"type":"box","kind":"look","t":"Regra","body":"Modal perfect em histórias cria **suspense**: do **talvez** (might) ao **quase certo** (must)."}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences","bank":null,"items":[{"s":"Someone ___ have taken it. (might)","a":"might","why":"might have."},{"s":"She could have ___ it in the car. (leave, part.)","a":"left","why":"particípio."},{"s":"It ___ have fallen behind the desk. (may)","a":"may","why":"may have."},{"s":"It can’t have ___ . (vanish, part.)","a":"vanished","why":"particípio."}]},{"type":"match","title":"Match the word to its meaning","pairs":[["misplaced speech","discurso extraviado"],["coat pocket","bolso do casaco"],["mayor’s aide","assessora do prefeito"],["office search","busca no escritório"],["desk drawer","gaveta de mesa"]]},{"type":"order","title":"Put the words in order","items":[{"words":["gone","Where","could","the","speech","have"],"ans":"Where could the speech have gone","pt":"Para onde o discurso poderia ter ido?"},{"words":["behind","the","desk","It","might","have","fallen"],"ans":"It might have fallen behind the desk","pt":"Pode ter caído atrás da mesa."}]}]},{"tag":"Vocabulário","title":"Words and expressions","blocks":[{"type":"vocab","items":[{"w":"misplaced speech","pos":"word","pt":"discurso extraviado","ex":"Misplaced speech.","expt":"Discurso extraviado."},{"w":"coat pocket","pos":"word","pt":"bolso do casaco","ex":"Coat pocket.","expt":"Bolso do casaco."},{"w":"mayor’s aide","pos":"word","pt":"assessora do prefeito","ex":"Mayor’s aide.","expt":"Assessora do prefeito."},{"w":"office search","pos":"word","pt":"busca no escritório","ex":"Office search.","expt":"Busca no escritório."},{"w":"speech draft","pos":"word","pt":"rascunho do discurso","ex":"Speech draft.","expt":"Rascunho do discurso."},{"w":"podium note","pos":"word","pt":"nota de pódio","ex":"Podium note.","expt":"Nota de pódio."},{"w":"campaign car","pos":"word","pt":"carro de campanha","ex":"Campaign car.","expt":"Carro de campanha."},{"w":"panic moment","pos":"word","pt":"momento de pânico","ex":"Panic moment.","expt":"Momento de pânico."},{"w":"lost document","pos":"word","pt":"documento perdido","ex":"Lost document.","expt":"Documento perdido."},{"w":"secretary’s desk","pos":"word","pt":"mesa da secretária","ex":"Secretary’s desk.","expt":"Mesa da secretária."},{"w":"tidy shelf","pos":"word","pt":"prateleira arrumada","ex":"Tidy shelf.","expt":"Prateleira arrumada."},{"w":"hallway whisper","pos":"word","pt":"sussurro no corredor","ex":"Hallway whisper.","expt":"Sussurro no corredor."},{"w":"city hall corridor","pos":"word","pt":"corredor da prefeitura","ex":"City hall corridor.","expt":"Corredor da prefeitura."},{"w":"ceremony delay","pos":"word","pt":"atraso da cerimônia","ex":"Ceremony delay.","expt":"Atraso da cerimônia."},{"w":"mistaken guess","pos":"word","pt":"palpite errado","ex":"Mistaken guess.","expt":"Palpite errado."},{"w":"funny ending","pos":"word","pt":"final engraçado","ex":"Funny ending.","expt":"Final engraçado."},{"w":"story clue","pos":"word","pt":"pista da história","ex":"Story clue.","expt":"Pista da história."},{"w":"plot suspense","pos":"word","pt":"suspense do enredo","ex":"Plot suspense.","expt":"Suspense do enredo."},{"w":"short fiction","pos":"word","pt":"ficção curta","ex":"Short fiction.","expt":"Ficção curta."},{"w":"opening line","pos":"word","pt":"primeira frase","ex":"Opening line.","expt":"Primeira frase."}]},{"type":"box","kind":"culture","t":"Expressões desta aula","body":["**Out of the blue.** — De repente.","**Lost the plot.** — Perder o fio da meada.","**Laugh it off.** — Levar na brincadeira.","**A wild goose chase.** — Uma busca inútil.","**Turn up.** — Aparecer.","**Cross my mind.** — Passar pela minha cabeça.","**Where could the speech have gone?** — Para onde o discurso poderia ter ido?","**It might have fallen behind the desk.** — Pode ter caído atrás da mesa.","**Or she may have left it in the car.** — Ou ela pode ter deixado no carro."]}]},{"tag":"Verbos","title":"Verbs in focus","blocks":[{"type":"verbs","items":[{"v":"vanish","pt":"desaparecer","forms":[["I / you / we / they vanish","The papers vanish."],["he / she / it vanishes","Os papéis desaparecem."]]}]}]},{"tag":"Escuta e diálogo","title":"Story club","blocks":[{"type":"dialog","title":"Story club","lines":[["Ana","Where could the speech have gone?","Para onde o discurso poderia ter ido?"],["Leo","It might have fallen behind the desk.","Pode ter caído atrás da mesa."],["Ana","Or she may have left it in the car.","Ou ela pode ter deixado no carro."],["Leo","No, she must have put it in her coat.","Não, ela deve tê-lo colocado no casaco."]]},{"type":"pron","title":"Pronúncia: Flap T americano","items":[{"label":"Flap T americano","note":"Entre vogais o /t/ americano vira um toque rápido /ɾ/: water, better, city, got it.","words":["water","better","city","got it","a lot of"]}]}]},{"tag":"Fala","title":"Speaking","blocks":[{"type":"speak","title":"Speaking","prompts":[{"q":"Guess what happened.","pt":"Adivinhe.","model":"It might have fallen."},{"q":"Say something was impossible.","pt":"Diga.","model":"It can’t have disappeared."},{"q":"Draw a strong conclusion.","pt":"Conclua.","model":"She must have put it there."}]}]},{"tag":"Escrita","title":"Writing","blocks":[{"type":"write","task":"Write a 6-sentence mini story using might/could/may have, can’t have and must have.","model":"My keys were gone. I might have left them at work, or I could have dropped them on the bus. They can’t have disappeared from the house. Then I found them in my coat. I must have put them there. We laughed about it.","checklist":["Usei **might/could have**","Usei **can’t have**","Usei **must have**"],"words":"6 frases"}]},{"tag":"Revisão e exame","title":"Review · Exam strategy · Teacher’s note","blocks":[{"type":"mcq","title":"Check yourself","items":[{"q":"What does “misplaced speech” mean?","opts":["bolso do casaco","busca no escritório","discurso extraviado"],"ans":2,"why":"**misplaced speech** = discurso extraviado."},{"q":"